WEBVTT

00:00:28.621 --> 00:00:33.329
All around the world, countless people 
are doing this every second—

00:00:33.329 --> 00:00:37.704
flipping a switch, plugging in, 
pressing an “on” button.

00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:41.621
So how much electricity 
does humanity need?

00:00:41.621 --> 00:00:44.912
The amount we collectively use
is changing fast,

00:00:44.912 --> 00:00:46.162
so to answer this question,

00:00:46.162 --> 00:00:49.704
we need to know not just how much 
the world uses today,

00:00:49.704 --> 00:00:52.412
but how much we’ll use in the future.

00:00:53.079 --> 00:00:57.121
The first step is understanding
how we measure electricity.

00:00:57.121 --> 00:00:58.537
It’s a little bit tricky.

00:00:58.537 --> 00:01:00.829
A joule is a unit of energy,